## Before code

Abstract "implement page X" is invalid without an explicit operator spec. Contracts live in `ui.mdc`, `frontend-modular.mdc`, and `api/openapi/`.

## AI laziness and dishonesty (admin UI)

Agents optimize for plausible diffs, not operator intent. Treat these as **lie modes** (`anti-slop.mdc`).

| Failure mode | What agents do | Required behavior |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Doc ask -> code | Operator asks for `.mdc` update; agent edits components | Write rules only unless operator asked to implement |
| Piecemeal teardown | Delete or refactor `web/` file-by-file; half tree + broken CI | Remove or recreate `web/` atomically per operator direction; server embed stays in `internal/controlplane/admin_static_stub/` |
| History restore | Copy pre-reset `web/` from git without `ui.mdc` contract | Forbidden; rebuild from rules + OpenAPI + cold path |
| Wrapper stack | `*DirectoryChrome`, `*Workspace`, `*Cluster` over grid | One section = one `ui/<domain>/` folder; page composes sections |
| Flex/portrait layout | Flex on page/section; portal listbox for filter fields | CSS Grid sections only; field listboxes inline (`Dropdowns` below) |
| Phantom contract | "See prior width contract" with no table in repo | Contract must live in this file |
| Unrun verification | "typecheck passed", "admin_web green" | Paste command + package path + outcome (`quality.mdc`) |
| Client logic smuggle | `useMemo` filter/sort over full API payload | Server query params; browser renders page |
| Filter pagination relocation | Operator asks to move Prev/Next into filter grid; agent wraps or moves **Apply** | **Directory filter row and pagination** below; Apply stays direct grid child |
| Double chip chrome | `PageHeader` wrapper + `FreshnessBadge` border | Parent slot renders chip directly (`Chips` below) |
| Boot HTML drift | Text inside `<div id="root">` | Empty `<div id="root"></div>` only; boot inject in `admin_ui_static.go` |

Rejected slice: revert; do not add compensating wrappers.

## Cold path first (non-negotiable)

Browser **renders** server output. Logic stays in Go.

| Concern | Server | Browser |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Filter / search | Query params; SQL/CH in handler | Send params; show `items`, `total` |
| Sort | `sort`, `order` on API | Refetch |
| Pagination | `limit`, `offset` or cursor | Controls only |
| List envelope | `items`, `total`, `limit`, `offset`, `freshness`, `filters_applied`, `sort` on directory handlers (`ListEnvelope` OpenAPI) | Refetch on param change; no client envelope math |
| KPIs / aggregates | Handler or report row fields | Display |
| Freshness | `stale`, `ch_lag_seconds`, prefer `freshness_label` | Chip text from API; no client lag math |
| Money | Micros + currency or `*_display` from API | Format display fields only |
| Status | `status`, `status_label`, `status_tone` | Map tone enum to chip |
| Export | Server export endpoint or async job | Download link |
| Validation | 400 + field errors from handler | Show API errors |

Forbidden in new `web/src/helpers/`: client-side filter/sort/reduce over full datasets; duplicated report keys; business rules that belong in handlers.

**Rule:** need a derived field -> add to handler DTO in the same PR as the UI page.

