## Layout (CSS Grid only)

From `admin_shell` onward. Page = grid of sections. Section owns `grid-template-columns`. Controls are leaves.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Section owns template | `grid-template-columns` / `rows` only on section root |
| Controls are leaves | No `margin-left: auto` escaping the cell |
| One chrome per region | One `PageChrome`, one filter section, one data section, one footer |
| Rhythm | `row-gap` / `column-gap` on section grid; not margin stacks between sections |
| Z-index | Open dropdown: cell z-index; section `position: relative` when `[data-dropdown-open]` |
| Subgrid | Data grid: one column template; body rows `grid-column: 1 / -1; subgrid` |

Forbidden for page layout:

- `display: flex` on page, section, toolbar, footer
- `display: table*` / `<table>` for data
- `position: fixed` filter panels blocking content (inline accordion in flow only)
- Parallel layout systems (flex page + grid table + portal toolbar)
- Extra wrapper components that only add chrome (`*Chrome` around `*Chrome`)

### Section stack

`ContextBar` -> `PageChrome` -> `Toolbar` -> `[FilterPanel]` -> `Content` -> `Footer`.

### Directory filter row and pagination

Operator ask: move **Prev/Next** from list footer into the **filter grid** (bottom-right cell). That is **not** permission to relocate **Apply** or invent a second filter layout.

Canonical reference: `web/src/ui/billing/billing_filter.tsx` (Apply only); `web/src/ui/campaigns/campaigns_filter.tsx` (Apply + pagination).

#### Filter row contract

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One `.filterRow` grid | `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(12rem, 1fr))`; `align-items: end` |
| Field cells | Each filter is a `.filterField` label block (same as billing) |
| **Apply** | Direct child of `.filterRow`, **after** the last filter field (`Order`, etc.); plain `<Button type="submit">`; **no wrapper** |
| **Prev/Next** | Separate direct child of `.filterRow`, **after** Apply; `PaginationPrevNext` with `className` for column width only |
| Column width | Pagination root `width: 100%` of its grid cell; inner `grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr` splits Prev/Next with gap |
| Button height | Match field controls (`var(--control-height-md)`, `var(--text-sm)`) — not compact `text-xs` slivers |
| Footer | Remove duplicate `PaginationBar` from directory footer when pagination lives in filter row |

DOM order (campaigns-shaped directory):

```
.filterRow
  .filterField × N   (customer, status, …, sort, order)
  Button[Apply]      ← unchanged slot
  PaginationPrevNext ← new cell to the right; does not wrap Apply
```

#### Agent failure modes (forbidden)

| What agents do | Why it is wrong | Correct |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Split `filters` into `filterFields` + `filterEnd` column | Moves Apply out of the filter grid into a side column | Single `.filterRow`; all children are peers |
| Wrap Apply + pagination in `filterEndCap` / `filterActions` | Groups controls; shrinks or shifts Apply | Apply and pagination are **sibling** grid items |
| Second row (`filterRowBottom`) for Sort/Order/Apply | Breaks original row flow; operator sees Apply "moved" | Keep Sort/Order in the same `.filterRow` as other fields |
| Stack Prev/Next **above** Apply | Operator asked for horizontal pair in the grid corner, not a vertical tower | Pagination is its **own** cell beside Apply, not stacked on it |
| `margin-left: auto` on a wrapper containing Apply | Pushes Apply away from its column after Order | No auto margin on Apply; optional `justify-self` only on pagination cell if the page catalog specifies |
| Fixed `width: 5.75rem` + `justify-self: end` on pagination | Tiny buttons floating in empty grid space | `width: 100%`; fill the auto-fill column like other fields |
| Touch Apply styling/position when task is "add pagination" | Operator said pagination moves; Apply stays | Diff Apply line should be **zero** unless explicitly requested |

**Read operator layout literally:** "bottom-right corner of the filter grid" = last **grid cell** on the wrap row, not a new layout system. "Width like Apply" = width of the **grid column** Apply sits in, split 50/50 for Prev/Next — not a arbitrary `rem` constant narrower than the column.

Rejected slice: revert wrapper/column/second-row changes; restore billing-shaped Apply; add pagination as the next sibling only.

## Data grid (no `<table>`)

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| Root | `role="grid"`; `role="row"` / `columnheader` / `gridcell` |
| Columns | One `grid-template-columns` on `.dataGrid`; header + rows share via subgrid |
| Widths | Define once as `--<profile>-cols`; name `minmax(8rem, 1.4fr)`; fixed cols in `rem` |
| Empty / loading | Single cell `grid-column: 1 / -1`; skeleton uses same column template |

Column alignment:

| Kind | `justify-items` |
| :--- | :--- |
| name, money, numeric, cost_center | `start` |
| status, chargeback, created, campaigns, actions | `center` |

Status chips: fixed `rem` width in column so labels align.

## Chips and badges (strict)

Defect class: pills like **Lag unknown** with **unequal inset** or **nested frames** (gray outer box around colored inner pill). Example failure: `.titleBadge` wrapping `FreshnessBadge`.

| Rule | Detail |
| :--- | :--- |
| One chrome layer | Chip owns border, fill, padding; parent renders chip directly |
| Symmetric inset | Same token all sides (`padding: var(--space-1)`); forbidden `padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-2)`, `0.125rem var(--space-2)`, `0 var(--space-2)` |
| Vertical center | `inline-grid`, `align-items: center`, `line-height: var(--text-caption-leading)`; not ad-hoc `line-height: 1.2` |
| No nested frames | One `.root`; no wrapper border around semantic chip |
| Labels from API | Prefer `freshness_label`, `status_label` from handler |

## Dropdowns

| Kind | Mount | Width |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Field listbox | Inline `.drop` on `.wrap` / `.anchor` with `width: 100%` | Wrapper box in grid cell |
| Popover (hint, inbox, row overflow) | `AnchorOverlay` portal | `max(anchor, content)` with care |

### Field listbox width contract

| Failure | Cause | Fix |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Menu **narrower** than field | Width on `<button>`; button shrinks to label in grid cell | Wrapper `width: 100%`; `.drop { left: 0; right: 0; width: 100% }` |
| Menu **wider** than pagination trigger | Portal + `Math.max(anchor, content)`; measure inflated (~192px) | Field listboxes: no portal, no content measure |
| Menu **clipped** | Filter section `overflow: hidden` | `overflow: visible` when `[data-dropdown-open]` |

Popover width rules do **not** apply to toolbar/filter `Select` / `FilterDropdown`.

## Fetch and error UI

List/grid allocation and scroll budgets: `react.mdc` (DoD, prefetch, GC).

| State | Condition | UI |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Initial load | `fetching && !data && !error` | `PageSkeleton` / grid skeleton |
| Blocking error | `error && !data` | `ErrorBlock` / `ErrorView`; no empty table |
| Stale revalidate | `data` present + error | Keep rows; toast or `AlertBanner` |
| Timeout | 15 s (`RESOURCE_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS`) | Clear `fetching` in `finally` |
| Mutation | PATCH/POST | `apiConfirmed`; toast only after 2xx |
| Empty | `items.length === 0`, filters inactive | `EmptyState` + one sentence |

No silent `catch` -> empty table. No `live: true` without `/api/v1`.

